Subject: [PATCH 02219/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE B1 (CLOSE
 THE IN-GENERATION MOAT; rebuild the underpowered exp4304 w/ a stronger
 architecture) -- DiffusionGemma in-generation, external-PRM REWARD-GUIDED
 STEP-STITCHING, must-beat the self-reward SMC intrinsic baseline. .398
 (exp4304) had a CLEAN harness (controls_differentiated=true,
 scorer_leak_recheck_passed=true) and a POSITIVE point estimate
 (carnot_minus_best_control_delta +0.133) but CI95 [-0.067,0.367] INCLUDED 0
 (underpowered, NOT refuted). The .399 sweep flagged the architecture upgrade:
 instead of a single guided pass, use REWARD-GUIDED STITCHING
 (arXiv:2602.22871) -- sample DIVERSE diffusion reasoning trajectories, score
 EVERY intermediate step with the exp4292 external partial-state scorer, and
 STITCH the highest-scoring steps into a composite (+23.8% in the paper).
 CRITICAL must-beat baseline (arXiv:2602.01849, the .399 sweep): SELF-REWARD
 SMC -- a particle filter using the model's OWN trajectory self-confidence (NO
 external scorer) -- so the moat now means Carnot's EXTERNAL verifier beats
 the model's INTRINSIC self-confidence -- the sharpest oracle-distinct test in
 generation. Keep: (1) an INDEPENDENT leak re-check on the exp4292 scorer, (2)
 >=1 genuinely-engaged non-Carnot control (RFG enhanced!=reference at gamma>0,
 2509.25604, OR EntRGi 2602.05000) + the exp4308 DEGENERATE_CONTROLS no-op
 guard, (3) MORE power (n>=40 per arm). Emit diffusiongemma_guidance_moat BARE
 bool := (Carnot-stitched - best-engaged-control > 0 AND CI95-excl-0 AND
 controls_differentiated AND beats self-reward SMC). verifier_is_oracle=false.
 NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; DiffusionGemma via the llama.cpp
 PR binary.

